##DESCRIPTION
## Trigonometry reference angles in radians
##ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Trigonometry)
## DBchapter(Geometric and algebraic foundations for trigonometry)
## DBsection(Reference angles (using coterminal angles))
## Date(January 2012)
## Institution(Mississippi College)
## Author(John Travis)
## MLT(KentMoreLike3)
## Level(3)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('Trigonometry')
## AuthorText1('')
## EditionText1('')
## Section1('.')
## Problem1('')
## KEYWORDS('radians','reference angles','unit circle','trigonometry')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserPopUp.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$a = random(2, 5);
if ($a == 2) {
    $ans_a1 = "II";
    $ans_a2 = Compute("pi - $a");
    $ans_a3 = "\pi - $a";
} elsif ($a == 3) {
    $ans_a1 = "II";
    $ans_a2 = Compute("pi - $a");
    $ans_a3 = "\pi - $a";
} elsif ($a == 4) {
    $ans_a1 = "III";
    $ans_a2 = Compute("$a-pi");
    $ans_a3 = "$a - \pi";
} else {
    $ans_a1 = "IV";
    $ans_a2 = Compute("2 pi - $a");
    $ans_a3 = "2\pi - $a";
}

$b = random(6, 9);
if ($b == 6) {
    $ans_b1 = "IV";
    $ans_b2 = Compute("2 * pi - $b");
    $ans_b3 = "2\pi - $b";
}
if ($b == 7) {
    $ans_b1 = "I";
    $ans_b2 = Compute("-2 * pi + $b");
    $ans_b3 = "$b - 2\pi";
}
if ($b == 8) {
    $ans_b1 = "I";
    $ans_b2 = Compute("-2 * pi + $b");
    $ans_b3 = "$b - 2\pi";
}
if ($b == 9) {
    $ans_b1 = "II";
    $ans_b2 = Compute("3 * pi - $b");
    $ans_b3 = "3\pi - $b";
}

$c = random(10, 13, 1);
if ($c == 10) {
    $ans_c1 = "III";
    $ans_c2 = Compute("-3 * $pi + $c");
    $ans_c3 = "$c - 3\pi";
}
if ($c == 11) {
    $ans_c1 = "IV";
    $ans_c2 = Compute("4 * $pi - $c");
    $ans_c3 = "4\pi - $c";
}
if ($c == 12) {
    $ans_c1 = "IV";
    $ans_c2 = Compute("4 * $pi - $c");
    $ans_c3 = "4\pi - $c";
}
if ($c == 13) {
    $ans_c1 = "I";
    $ans_c2 = Compute("-4 * $pi + $c");
    $ans_c3 = "$c - 4\pi";
}

$d = random(-10, -4, 2);
if ($d == -10) {
    $ans_d1 = "II";
    $ans_d2 = Compute("-3 pi - $d");
    $ans_d3 = "|-4\pi - $d|";
}
if ($d == -8) {
    $ans_d1 = "IV";
    $ans_d2 = Compute("-2 pi - $d");
    $ans_d3 = "|-2\pi - $d|";
}
if ($d == -6) {
    $ans_d1 = "I";
    $ans_d2 = Compute("2 pi + $d");
    $ans_d3 = "|-2\pi - $d|";
}
if ($d == -4) {
    $ans_d1 = "II";
    $ans_d2 = Compute("-pi - $d");
    $ans_d3 = "|-\pi - $d|";
}

$popup_a = DropDown([ "I", "II", "III", "IV" ], $ans_a1);
$popup_b = DropDown([ "I", "II", "III", "IV" ], $ans_b1);
$popup_c = DropDown([ "I", "II", "III", "IV" ], $ans_c1);
$popup_d = DropDown([ "I", "II", "III", "IV" ], $ans_d1);

BEGIN_PGML
For each angle below, determine the quadrant in which the terminal side of the
angle is found and find the corresponding reference angle [` \bar { \theta }`].

You can enter [` \pi `] as 'pi' in your answers.

a) [` \theta = [$a] `] is found in quadrant [_]{$popup_a} 
and [` \bar { \theta } = `] [_]{$ans_a2}

b) [` \theta = [$b] `]is found in quadrant [_]{$popup_b} and
[` \bar { \theta } = `] [_]{$ans_b2}

c) [` \theta = [$c] `] is found in quadrant [_]{$popup_c} and
[` \bar { \theta } = `] [_]{$ans_c2}

d) [` \theta = [$d] `] is found in quadrant [_]{$popup_d} and
[` \bar { \theta } = `] [_]{$ans_d2}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_HINT

For a given angle [` \theta  `], the reference angle is the acute angle found by taking the difference between [` \theta  `] and the nearest horizontal axes. 
  
First, determine the quadrant in which [` \theta  `] lies.
  
Next, remember that in radians the horizontal angles are all multiples of [`\pi`].
END_PGML_HINT

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
The correct answers are 

a) [` \theta = [$a] `] is found in quadrant [_]{$popup_a}
with reference angle [`[$ans_a3] = [$ans_a2]`],

b) [` \theta = [$b] `] is found in quadrant [_]{$popup_b}
with reference angle [`[$ans_b3] = [$ans_b2]`],

c) [` \theta = [$c] `] is found in quadrant [_]{$popup_c}
with reference angle [`[$ans_c3] = [$ans_c2]`].

d) When the angle is negative, the "x-axis" angles are [`0, -\pi, -2\pi,`] etc.  One must take care on dealing with signs so it might be easiest to just state formulas with absolute values.

    [` \theta = [$d] `] is found in quadrant [_]{$popup_d}
    with reference angle [`[$ans_d3] = [$ans_d2]`].
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();       